From 59fe921566ac8666f04c2c47ae1d7a9f14a6f90b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Fesunenko <body051@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 20:43:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] stm32: Add parallel (FSMC) TFT display and XPT2046 touch
 support

Add a "tft_fsmc" module for STM32F4 that drives MIPI DCS compatible
displays on the FSMC bus with simple drawing primitives: controller
commands, solid fills, scaled monochrome bitmaps and an RLE encoded
pixel stream.  Also add a software SPI reader for XPT2046 resistive
touch controllers.  A touch read is done one conversion per task run so
it never blocks other work for long.  The drawing and touch commands are
allowed after a shutdown so a host can keep showing (and using) the
screen.

Used for the touch screens of Lerdge boards.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
